{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":342453,"ns":0,"title":"Center (algebra)","extract":"The term center or centre is used in various contexts in abstract algebra to denote the set of all those elements that commute with all other elements.\n\nThe center of a group G consists of all those elements x in G such that xg = gx for all g in G. This is a normal subgroup of G.\nThe similarly named notion for a semigroup is defined likewise and it is a subsemigroup.","description":"Index of articles associated with the same name","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}